-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a4ab5110-53f8-5536-b8d4-ee00d53d6350
-- title:
--   A test function vanishing on the supersingular component, q=3
-- statement:
--   The setting is the following. A prime $q$ with $q=3$ is fixed, together with a non-zero level $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` is given, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. of the places $w$ which are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ whose integers form a principal ideal ring, and $P.\mathrm{ord}$ is the associated normalised order function, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ the evaluation obtained by inverting $K \to$ residue field of $P$.
--
--   The field `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\!\left(\!\left(t\right)\!\right)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base-changed full level-$M'$ modular function field into it; `IntermediateField.inclusion hle` denotes the resulting embedding. Throughout, $\hat\jmath$ denotes the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of the rational $j$-expansion `jq`.
--
--   A constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with target `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is given: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ extending $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, in which every non-zero element becomes, after scaling by a constant, an integral element of non-zero residue, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that $R_0$ is the coefficientwise (Gauss) reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}\!\left(\!\left(t\right)\!\right)$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   An element $\zeta$ of `Idx q`, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is fixed, and two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: the Igusa family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the points of [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $= \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and the family $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. They satisfy the following groups of hypotheses. The hypothesis `hIg_inf` describes $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the point `lineInfty q` (the class of $(1,0)$): $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ to `ResidueField A` is non-zero and $f$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}\!\left(\!\left(t\right)\!\right)$. The hypothesis `hIg` asserts that for every point $\mathcal L$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ whose reduction `redQ q γ` carries `lineInfty q` to $\mathcal L$ and for which $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\mathcal L}$ is the preimage of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ under the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ attached to $\zeta$ and $\gamma$; `hIg_inj` asserts that $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` asserts that for every $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ with $(O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\mathcal L})$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\sigma \mathcal L}$ for all $\mathcal L$.
--
--   For the supersingular family: `hSS_A` says that for each $s$ and each $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ the image of $x$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ if and only if $x \in A$. The hypothesis `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\hat\jmath$ is regular, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, one has: the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and of $a$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ and in its maximal ideal. The hypothesis `hSS_fix` says that each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ is its own preimage under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and `hSS_tr` that for each $s$ there is $t \in O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   One place $s \in W$ is then fixed, together with a field $F^{\mathrm{SS}}$ which is an algebra over `ResidueField A`, a component chart $C_b$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with values in $F^{\mathrm{SS}}$ whose integers are $O^{\mathrm{SS}}_s$ (`hCb`), and the hypothesis `htr` that $F^{\mathrm{SS}}$ contains an element transcendental over `ResidueField A`. Two families of annuli $\mathrm{An}'$ and $\mathrm{An}$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ are given, together with an injective family $\mathrm{xt}$ of places of $F^{\mathrm{SS}}$ over `ResidueField A` (`hxt_inj`). The hypothesis `hAn` states, for each $\mathcal L$, that $\mathrm{An}'_{\mathcal L}$ and $\mathrm{An}_{\mathcal L}$ have the same domain and the same modulus, that this modulus is non-zero in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and that the product of the two parameters is the image of the modulus, so that the two annuli are reciprocal. The hypothesis `hxt_att` states, in terms of the regular prolongation determined by the integers and residue map of $C_b$, that for each $\mathcal L$ the parameter of $\mathrm{An}'_{\mathcal L}$ is integral, its residue has order $1$ at $\mathrm{xt}_{\mathcal L}$, and for every integral $f$ with non-zero residue and with $\mathrm{ord}_P f = 0$ at all $P$ in the domain of $\mathrm{An}'_{\mathcal L}$, the product of $P.\mathrm{evalAt} f$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the parameter raised to minus the order at $\mathrm{xt}_{\mathcal L}$ of the residue of $f$ lies in $A$ and is a unit there; this is the attachment condition without the clause that $\mathrm{xt}_{\mathcal L}$ be a node of the chart. The hypothesis `hAn_tube` places the annulus places in the tube over $s$: for each $\mathcal L$, each $P$ in the domain of $\mathrm{An}'_{\mathcal L}$ and each $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular wherever $\hat\jmath$ is regular and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a \in A$ whose residue is the value of that residue at $s$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   Finally, an element $J$ of `fieldBar q M'` is given whose Laurent expansion is `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`, the $j$-expansion with the variable replaced by its $q$-th power (`hJ`), which by `hJreg` is regular at every place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of $\hat\jmath$ is regular. The Hasse datum `hHasse` provides: a constant $a_0 \in A$ such that $J - a_0$ lies in the integers of $C_b$ with $C_b$-residue $0$; a constant $c' \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ such that $c' \cdot (J - a_0)$ lies in the integers of $C_b$ with non-zero $C_b$-residue; and, for every point $\mathcal L$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, a field $F^{\mathrm{I}}$ which is an algebra over `ResidueField A`, a component chart $C$ of `fieldBar q M'` along $A$ with values in $F^{\mathrm{I}}$ and a place $x$ of $F^{\mathrm{I}}$ over `ResidueField A` such that the integers of $C$ are $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\mathcal L}$, the annulus $\mathrm{An}_{\mathcal L}$ is attached to $C$ at $x$ (that is, $x$ is a node of $C$, the parameter of $\mathrm{An}_{\mathcal L}$ is $C$-integral with residue of order $1$ at $x$, and the unit condition above holds for $C$, $x$ and $\mathrm{An}_{\mathcal L}$), and $J - a_0$ is $C$-integral with non-zero $C$-residue and $$\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{xt}_{\mathcal L}}\bigl(C_b\text{-residue of } c'(J-a_0)\bigr) \;=\; -\,\mathrm{ord}_{x}\bigl(C\text{-residue of } J-a_0\bigr).$$
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every point $\mathcal L$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ there exists $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` such that $g \neq 0$; $g$ is regular at every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of $\hat\jmath$ is regular, i.e. $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(\hat\jmath) \Rightarrow 0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$; $g$ lies in the integers of $C_b$ and its $C_b$-residue is $0$; both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ lie in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\mathcal L}$, so that $g$ is a unit of the Igusa ring at $\mathcal L$; and $P.\mathrm{ord}(g) = 0$ for every $P$ in the domain of $\mathrm{An}'_{\mathcal L}$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case, at an auxiliary level rigidified by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the production of a test function on the full-level modular curve that vanishes identically on the supersingular component, is a unit on each Igusa component and has no zeros or poles on the tube annuli; the function is produced from the $j$-invariant datum $J$ and the Hasse constant $a_0$. It feeds the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve with its charts and annuli, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
